Cillian: Good morning Noelle! What a lovely surprise seeing you return! #portrait:Cillian
Cillian: I was just talking with Rowan about you. #portrait:Cillian
Narrator: Rowan nods in acknowledgement.
Rowan: Morning, I assume you are still after the sail? #portrait:Rowan
Amelia: Still not wanting to make us one? #portrait:AmeliaAngry
Cillian: Actually Amelia, we were just discussing this. #portrait:Cillian
Cillian: I admire your bravery, and it's not like you’re asking very much. Rowan can complete the minimal stitching in an hour at most. #portrait:Cillian
Noelle: Yes. It’s meant to just be a simple one. But… I understand if you don’t have time. #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Narrator: You explain your decisions from last night, saying that even without a sail, you’d still be fine.
Noelle: But in the case of using my boat to transport goods around the island, if needed… a sail would definitely help things along quicker. #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Noelle: I can sew one by myself, of course — but both Cillian and Clara have been vouching for the quality of your work, so… #portrait:NoelleUm
Narrator: You trail off.
Noelle: Sorry for putting you in an awkward position. #portrait:NoelleUm
Narrator: Cillian smiles, happy with the developments you described. Rowan lets out a deep sigh, pinching his brow.
Cillian: So? #portrait:Cillian
Rowan: Ugh, fine. #portrait:Rowan
Rowan: But since I’ll be cooped up in my workshop, I’m going to need you to run an errand for me. #portrait:Rowan
